      <h2 id="types-heading" class="section-heading">Removable Overdentures vs. Fixed Hybrids</h2>
      <span class="gold-rule"></span>
      <p>Implant dentures come in two main forms. An overdenture snaps onto implants and can be removed by the patient for cleaning. A fixed hybrid prosthesis is screw-retained — it stays in permanently and is only removed by the provider.</p>
      <p>Which approach is right depends on your anatomy, bone volume, and goals. {{ site.doctorName }} will walk you through both options and recommend what fits your situation.</p>
    </div>
